<title>MALAYSIA: Southern Bank says seeks insurance arm.</title>
<headline>Southern Bank says seeks insurance arm.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysia's Southern Bank Bhd said on Wednesday it would look to acquire an insurance company in a move to diversify its operations.</p>
<p>&quot;We are looking for an insurance company, either in life, general or composite insurance,&quot; Tan Ghee Khay, Southern Bank's company secretary, told reporters after the company's annual general meeting.</p>
<p>Tan added, however, that no discussions were currently under way with any insurance company.</p>
<p>Tan also said the company would offer trade and manufacturing financing as additional products in the near future.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-206 2323)</p>
